          "base": {
            "audioFile": "m2_2_11_base.mp3",
            "words": 49,
            "approxSeconds": 21,
            "lines": [
              "The most common contaminant organisms are coagulase-negative staphylococci, which account for the majority.",
              "Corynebacterium species.",
              "Bacillus species, with the important exception of Bacillus anthracis, which is never dismissed as a contaminant.",
              "And Cutibacterium, formerly known as Propionibacterium.",
              "Proper aseptic technique is what keeps these organisms out of the bottle."
            ],
            "reveal": {
              "mode": "per_line",
              "note": "one cue per line, synced to the narration line beside it",
              "cues": [
