            "lines": [
              "Quality indicators are used to monitor the accuracy and effectiveness of blood culture collection.",
              "The contamination rate, which should be below 3 percent.",
              "Adequate blood volume - 8 to 10 millilitres per bottle in adults.",
              "Correct timing, meaning collection before the first dose of antibiotics.",
              "Timely transport, immediately and at room temperature.",
              "And proper labelling, at the bedside, with all four fields complete.",
              "Monitoring these indicators improves diagnostic accuracy, reduces errors and ensures high-quality patient care."
